[40.905034, "o", "AI reasoning:                                                                   \r\n                                                                                \r\nWe need to list pods in kube-system and indicate any unhealthy. Use             \r\nkubernetes_tabular_query to list pods with status.phase and ready condition? We \r\ncan query pods in namespace kube-system, columns:                               \r\nNAME:.metadata.name,PHASE:.status.phase,READY:.status.containerStatuses[].ready?\r\nMight need to aggregate. Simpler: get pods and then check conditions. Use       \r\nkubernetes_tabular_query with columns:                                          \r\nNAME:.metadata.name,PHASE:.status.phase,RESTARTS:.status.containerStatuses[].res\r\ntartCount? But we need unhealthy detection: pods not in Running phase or with   \r\nReady condition false. Could also fetch events. For now, list pods and note any \r\nnot Running.                                                                    \r\n                                                                                \r\nLet's query pods in kube-system.                                                \r\n                                                                                \r\n"]
[40.910041, "o", "Running tool #1 kubernetes_tabular_query: filter: kubectl get pods              \r\ncolumns=''NAME:.metadata.name,PHASE:.status.phase,READY:.status.conditions[?(@.t\r\nype==\"Ready\")].status'' (namespace=kube-system, label_selector=,                \r\nfield_selector=, filter=)                                                       \r\n"]
